  // shipped. What is left is true, so it is what is written.
  "pricing.included.heading": "What every plan includes",
  "pricing.included.paragraph.1": "Hosting. A website Orvay builds is served from our infrastructure on a subdomain we give you, so you need no server, no deployment and no domain of your own to have a site that answers. Connecting a domain you own is not built yet, and this page changes when it is.",
  "pricing.included.paragraph.2": "The governance engine, whole. Eight admission gates in a fixed order, an approval that is a scoped and bounded record rather than a checkbox, verification by an actor that did not do the work, and a hash-chained log of all of it. None of that is reduced on the free plan.",
  "pricing.included.paragraph.3": "Cost metering. What an action will cost is measured against your allowance before the action runs, so a refusal arrives before the spend rather than on a bill.",
  // Which limits are enforced by running code, said plainly. A pricing page that
  // describes limits nothing enforces is not lying to the customer's disadvantage,
  // and it is still describing software that does not exist.
  "pricing.enforcement.heading": "What is enforced today",
  "pricing.enforcement.paragraph.1": "The money allowance is enforced at the last admission gate, before any model is called. The number of runs a company may have in flight at once is not enforced anywhere yet: the limit is published and the code that would apply it is not written.",
  "pricing.enforcement.paragraph.2": "Prepaid packs are recorded but are not yet spent. The plan engine knows the rule, which is allowance first and then packs by soonest expiry, and no running part of the product loads a pack balance into it, so a pack bought today would sit unused rather than extend anything. Packs can be bought, so the buy controls are switched off on this deployment until that is fixed. This paragraph changes on the day that stops being true.",
  "pricing.enforcement.paragraph.3": "The member and department counts are limits the plan sets, and the admission gate compares them wherever the product supplies a count, which today is the invitation path alone. Plan features are not enforced anywhere yet, because nothing in the product asks for one, which is why every feature above says whether it exists.",
  "pricing.data.heading": "Where your data is",
  "pricing.data.paragraph.1": "The database is in Zurich, Switzerland. Switzerland is not in the European Union and not in the European Economic Area: it is a third country holding an adequacy decision from the European Commission, so a transfer from the EEA to us rests on that decision and needs no further instrument.",
  "pricing.data.paragraph.2": "Model inference is not in Switzerland. Text sent to a model vendor is processed in the United States under the standard contractual clauses in each vendor agreement. The privacy notice lists every sub-processor, what it receives and where it processes.",
  "pricing.data.paragraph.3": "We hold no certification of any kind and claim none. What is true and checkable is written above, and the sub-processor list is the place to check it.",
  "pricing.links.heading": "Read before you decide",
  "pricing.links.docs": "How credits and quota work, in more detail",
  "pricing.links.privacy": "Privacy notice",
  "pricing.links.terms": "Terms",
  "pricing.links.imprint": "Imprint",
  "pricing.cta.heading": "When it opens",
  "pricing.cta.body": "There is nothing to buy today. Leave an address and we will write once, when a plan can actually be bought.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // The language control
  //
  // The switcher renders in the language being switched FROM, because the person
  // reading it has not changed language yet. The OPTIONS are labelled with each
  // language's endonym from `LOCALES`, never translated, because a reader who
  // cannot read the current language cannot find their own in a list written in
  // it.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  "locale.label": "Language",
  "locale.submit": "Change",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Documentation navigation
  //
  // `apps/docs/src/nav.ts` keeps the SHAPE of the documentation, which is
  // structure: what exists, what nests under what, and the order a reader should
  // meet it in. The words that shape is labelled with are copy, and copy has one
  // owner. Keeping the two apart is what lets the sidebar be German without
  // `nav.ts` knowing any German.
  //
  // The key is derived from the slug, so adding a page to that tree makes `tsc`
  // demand two entries here rather than letting the page appear with a blank
  // label in the sidebar.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
