  "onboarding.purpose.refused": "The goal was not saved. Your company is set up and you can write the goal from the Goals page.",
  // 5 — Authority. A posture, recorded as an event. The rules themselves live on
  // the policies page, and the copy says so rather than implying this wrote them.
  "onboarding.authority.heading": "How much may an agent do on its own?",
  "onboarding.authority.body": "This sets where {brand} starts. Every action still leaves a record, and anything with a legal effect on a person always waits for a human.",
  "onboarding.authority.cautious.label": "Ask me first",
  "onboarding.authority.cautious.sublabel": "Nothing reaches an outside system without your approval, and a draft waits for you too.",
  "onboarding.authority.balanced.label": "Ask for the risky ones",
  "onboarding.authority.balanced.sublabel": "A draft runs and is verified. Anything public waits for you.",
  "onboarding.authority.open.label": "Act, and tell me",
  "onboarding.authority.open.sublabel": "Most actions run on their own. You review the record rather than the request.",
  // ON THE MOST PERMISSIVE OPTION, as words beside the glyph, because §7a rule 2
  // forbids colour or a shape being the only carrier of risk.
  //
  // It also states the one thing this posture does NOT do. A control promising to
  // skip every approval would be a lie: an action with a legal or similarly
